BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Faro//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Faro — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cataplana — Clams\, prawns\, fish and chouriço sealed in the hinged copper pot and steamed\, opened at the table.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ka-ta-PLA-na. The pot and the dish share one name\; a real one takes half an hour and arrives closed. Best: Tasca do Ricky\, Rua do Forno — order it when you sit down
LOCATION:Tasca do Ricky\, Rua do Forno — order it when you sit down
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tasca+do+Ricky+Rua+do+Forno+21+Faro+Portugal
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Arroz de lingueirão — A wet rice of the lagoon's razor clams\, served loose in its own broth.
DESCRIPTION:Say: a-ROSH de leen-gay-ROWNG. The Ria Formosa's own rice\, eaten from a spoon\, not a fork. Best: Estaminé\, on Ilha Deserta\, or Tasca do Ricky in the Baixa
LOCATION:Estaminé\, on Ilha Deserta\, or Tasca do Ricky in the Baixa
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tasca+do+Ricky+Rua+do+Forno+21+Faro+Portugal
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Amêijoas à Bulhão Pato — Lagoon clams opened in olive oil\, garlic\, coriander and lemon.
DESCRIPTION:Say: a-MAY-zhwash a bool-YOWNG PA-too. The simplest test of a kitchen that has good clams\; named for a 19th-century poet. Best: Tasca do Ricky\, Rua do Forno
LOCATION:Tasca do Ricky\, Rua do Forno
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tasca+do+Ricky+Rua+do+Forno+21+Faro+Portugal
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Polvo — Octopus\, grilled\, in a rice\, or cold in a salad with onion and coriander.
DESCRIPTION:Say: POL-voo. Santa Luzia\, by Tavira\, calls itself the octopus capital and still sets its traps in the lagoon. Best: Alameda in Faro\, or buy it at the Mercado de Olhão
LOCATION:Alameda in Faro\, or buy it at the Mercado de Olhão
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mercado+de+Olhao+Olh%C3%A3o+Portugal
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Sardinhas assadas — Sardines grilled whole over charcoal\, on bread that drinks the oil.
DESCRIPTION:Say: sar-DEEN-yash a-SA-dash. A summer dish: at their best from June\, and not something to order in November. Best: Adega Nova\, Rua Francisco Barreto — in summer\; frozen out of season
LOCATION:Adega Nova\, Rua Francisco Barreto — in summer\; frozen out of season
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Adega+Nova+Rua+Francisco+Barreto+Faro+Portugal
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Peixinhos da horta — Green beans fried in a light batter: ‘little fish from the garden’.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pay-SHEEN-yoosh da OR-ta. The fried bean often said to have gone to Japan as tempura\; the card on the curiosities tells it straight. Best: A Venda\, Rua do Compromisso — call in winter
LOCATION:A Venda\, Rua do Compromisso — call in winter
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=A+Venda+Rua+do+Compromisso+Faro+Portugal
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Bifana — Thin pork steak marinated in wine and garlic\, off the griddle into a crusty roll.
DESCRIPTION:Say: bee-FA-na. The town's breakfast and its standing lunch\, at a counter inside the market. Best: Snack Bar da Xica\, inside the Mercado Municipal — cash\, mornings
LOCATION:Snack Bar da Xica\, inside the Mercado Municipal — cash\, mornings
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mercado+Municipal+de+Faro+Portugal
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Dom Rodrigo — Egg-yolk threads\, almond and sugar\, wrapped in twisted coloured foil.
DESCRIPTION:Say: dong ro-DREE-goo. A convent sweet of the Algarve\, given a national protected name in December 2025. Best: Pastelaria Gardy\, Rua de Santo António
LOCATION:Pastelaria Gardy\, Rua de Santo António
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pastelaria+Gardy+Rua+de+Santo+Antonio+Faro+Portugal
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Flor de sal — The fine top crust of the salt pans\, skimmed by hand in summer.
DESCRIPTION:Say: flor de SAL. Tavira's sea salt carries a protected name\; a pinch on grilled fish is the point. Best: The Mercado de Olhão\, or the salt pans at Tavira
LOCATION:The Mercado de Olhão\, or the salt pans at Tavira
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mercado+de+Olhao+Olh%C3%A3o+Portugal
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Negra Mole — The Algarve's own red: pale\, soft\, fresh\, almost a rosé to look at.
DESCRIPTION:Say: NEH-gra MO-leh. An old grape the bulk-wine years nearly lost\, now made by a handful of growers. Best: Bago Wine Bar\, in the Baixa — ask for a Negra Mole from the Algarve
LOCATION:Bago Wine Bar\, in the Baixa — ask for a Negra Mole from the Algarve
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bago+Wine+Bar+Faro+Portugal
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Arinto — A white that keeps its lemon and its edge in the southern heat.
DESCRIPTION:Say: a-REEN-too. The glass the clams and the cataplana want. Best: With the clams at Tasca do Ricky
LOCATION:With the clams at Tasca do Ricky
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tasca+do+Ricky+Rua+do+Forno+21+Faro+Portugal
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Medronho — A clear spirit distilled from the red fruit of the strawberry tree in the hills of Monchique.
DESCRIPTION:Say: me-DRON-yoo. The digestif of the Algarve\; drink it at room temperature\, not iced. Best: After dinner at any tasca\; or the still at Marmelete\, in Monchique
LOCATION:After dinner at any tasca\; or the still at Marmelete\, in Monchique
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Marmelete+Monchique+Portugal
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Bica — A short black coffee\, drunk standing at the counter.
DESCRIPTION:Say: BEE-ka. The town's punctuation: one in the morning\, one after lunch\, one after dinner. Best: Café Aliança on the Jardim\, or Gardy
LOCATION:Café Aliança on the Jardim\, or Gardy
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pastelaria+Gardy+Rua+de+Santo+Antonio+Faro+Portugal
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:faro-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Figo e amêndoa — Dried figs and almonds of the barrocal\, the orchards behind the coast.
DESCRIPTION:Say: FEE-goo ee a-MEN-dwa. What the Algarve ate and sold before tourism\; in the markets all winter. Best: The Mercado Municipal de Faro\, in the morning
LOCATION:The Mercado Municipal de Faro\, in the morning
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mercado+Municipal+de+Faro+Portugal
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
